}
\details{
\strong{The control.} Give \code{control_type} the same value in the ui and the server call.
\itemize{
\item \code{"year"}: a chip listing the dataset's years (\code{cache()$data_years}), which starts on the first
of them. When the data has a \code{year} column, the table shows only the rows of the chosen year.
\item \code{"indicator"}: an indicator chip (\code{\link[=cd_indicator_ui]{cd_indicator_ui()}}) offering every indicator. The module
does not filter by it. The page reads the chosen indicator from the reactive the server returns
and builds \code{data} from it.
}

\strong{The columns.} These headings are translated without the page doing anything: \code{year},
\code{adminlevel_1}, \code{district} and \code{month}; columns whose name starts with \code{cov_} (coverage); columns
